      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I can see both parts in here.\nYou can't say that this update was completely useless, it made a lot of people come back to join random public worlds without the fear of crashing after 5 minutes. On the other hand i can see the problem with people becoming elitist for no reason. \n\nBut, this time, i think the problem is not entirely on the game, but more on the current community that can't use a feature for what is intended but for his own ego. \n\nMe and some friends always helped new people when we found them having problems with their first-second avatar in random avatar testing worlds, and then seeing them one week later with new stuff that they done by their own. If i was new and someone use this system for showing off his rank or block new people, well honestly i would be the first one to not wanting to deal with him.\n\nAnd in all honesty, this is not even a new thing: how many people were discriminating steam users before this?",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "5bbbd1b2cda04e5e4d302d7e",
      "author": {
        "_id": "5a396181ad0fe67038f895f9",
        "alias": "Mature Octopus",
        "aliasID": "65d35b800129d7ae44556744",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": null,
        "created": "2017-12-19T18:59:13.242Z",
        "name": "BigZeek",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": null
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "5ba416f404b76351bb808875",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2018-10-08T21:52:50.958Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "likeCount": 0,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5bb5a4eca1f2b571714fcfd7",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I hate to out myself, but, I have noticed in the last couple days I have blocked way more users than usual, and pretty much the majority of users I've blocked are Grey's.\n\nThe system let's me blocks Grey's everything for performance, which is nice, BUT, then, who wants to hang out, converse with default avatars. Not me. \n\nSecondarily, if I notice a world has more Grey's than greens and above, I'll just leave and try a different world. Without giving anyone there a chance because it's too obvious from the nameplates how many users there are grey. As well as I know this is a catch 23, but if I'm blocking everything from Grey's for performance, I don't want the be in a room full of default avatars, because again, I wouldn't be having fun then.\n\nThis is compounded then since I'm not having fun with Grey's if they are even slightly annoying I'll block them which hurts their trust score keeping them in a grey hell.\n\nThe system is fundamentally flawed on many levels. In my particular case if the system even exists there's a catch 22 until I can play VrChat without my headset loosing tracking randomly, but even if I did have grays avatars enabled, I probably still would objectively avoid Grey's because it's too obvious and the nameplates make them have a target on their heads.\n\nIf the system must remain, all nameplates should be green and have their detail page indicate their rank.\n\nAgain, hate to out myself, I don't consider myself an elitist,I consider myself just average gamer, then there are likely many, many others doing the same.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
